# OpenKraken — non-root access to NZXT devices (Arch Linux variant).
#
# BOTH lines are required: "hidraw" covers cooling/lighting/status (HID
# reports), and "usb" covers the LCD — a separate USB *bulk* interface driven
# through pyusb — plus device enumeration itself. Without the usb line
# liquidctl cannot read the string descriptors and enumeration dies with
# "The device has no langid (permission issue...)".
#
# Unlike the Debian rule this carries no MODE/GROUP: Arch has no plugdev group,
# and naming a group that does not exist makes udev log an error for every
# matching device. TAG+="uaccess" is enough on its own — systemd-logind puts an
# ACL for the user of the active local seat onto each node, which is exactly how
# liquidctl's own upstream rule (71-liquidctl.rules) grants access.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: uaccess follows the *active seat*, so a bare SSH
# session has no access even for the same user. Log in locally, or add your own
# GROUP= rule if you need headless control.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1e71", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1e71", TAG+="uaccess"
